{"book":10,"chapter":16,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / THE CORE OF THE LANGUAGE / CHAPTER 16","slides":[{"title":"A reference is a pointer","sub":"Chapter 16 · Borrowing instead of passing","short":"Intro","main":"A reference is eight bytes with an address; the check is at build time, free at run time.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Python","Rust","Eight bytes"],"captions":["In Python every name is already a reference to an object: the programmer never sees a separate \"reference\"","In Rust a reference is explicit: the ampersand takes the value's address, and the value stays with its owner","A reference is an ordinary pointer, eight bytes; the borrow checker works at build time, a reference costs nothing at run time"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":40.0,"w":40.0,"h":24.0,"text":"a","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":60.0,"y":90.0,"w":40.0,"h":24.0,"text":"b","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":240.0,"y":64.0,"w":110.0,"h":40.0,"text":"list","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":80.0,"y1":40.0,"x2":184.0,"y2":56.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":80.0,"y1":90.0,"x2":184.0,"y2":72.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"names are references to the object","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let s = String::from(\"hi\");","let r = &s;"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":17.0,"w":200.0},{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":290.0,"y":40.0,"w":80.0,"h":34.0,"text":"s\nowner","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":290.0,"y":112.0,"w":80.0,"h":34.0,"text":"r: &String\nborrow","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":290.0,"y1":94.0,"x2":290.0,"y2":58.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":80.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"r: &String\n0x7ffe…a0","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_si